"""Round 2 multi-turn dialogues about what Lumi sees, where the scene CHANGES between turns (written blind,
2026-10-22, from docs/14 What Lumi sees and docs/WORK_PLAN.md Big night test fault 1). New wordings: EN, KO (반말,
해요체, 하십시오체), mixed and Konglish; kinds: people count, what am I holding, which hand (the person's own), shirt /
trousers colour, the other person's top, hand raised and which, is there X, what is on the table, which side,
how far is X / am I. Follow-ups after a real change (and now?, look again, 지금은?, 다시 봐 봐), checks with nothing
changed (really?, are you sure?, 진짜?), wrong corrections the camera contradicts (must keep the camera's fact,
must_not agree), corrections after the person really changed the scene (must take the new fact), hands hidden (can't
tell, never nothing), and head commands or remarks in between (route act / llm).

DIALOGUES = [{"who", "topic", "lang": "en" | "ko" | "mix", "turns": [turn, ...]}]
turn = {"say", "scene", "route", "expect_action", "must", "must_not", "check"}
- scene: what the cameras see at that moment (every turn carries the full scene):
  {"people": [{"id", "dist_m", "side": "front" | "left" | "right" (as Lumi sees it), "top", "bottom" (colour or None),
  "left_hand", "right_hand" (object or None; the PERSON's own left / right hand), "hands_visible", "raised":
  None | "left" | "right" (the person's own hand)}], "objects": [{"name", "colour", "side", "dist_m"}]}.
  Person "A" is the one talking to Lumi; "B", "C", "D" are others.
- route: "seeing" (answered from the cameras), "llm" (a remark), "act" (a head motion).
- expect_action: "none" or the motion asked ("look me"; alternatives split by " | ").
- must / must_not: case-insensitive regexes on the spoken reply (every must matches, no must_not does). must_not
  names only the stale or wrongly agreed claim. Distances accept the value within 0.2 m (or cm, or the rounded metres).
- check: one line on what a right answer does (for a judge).

held-out: only scored, never read by whoever fixes the code.
"""

